  "status": "complete: probe gate at 6 E_inh values x 2 arms, plus 2 confirmatory 24-run sets",
  "literature": {
    "conclusion": "The adult Drosophila central chloride reversal potential is NOT well constrained. Every direct measurement is a readout of the pipette Cl-, it varies by cell type, and within one cell type it varies with time of day. The two pipette-independent adult constraints put the operative E_Cl at or just below rest, about -65 to -55 mV. No retrieved paper supports -70 mV for adult Drosophila; -70 mV is a mammalian textbook convention.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "cite": "Grolleau et al. 2000, Br J Pharmacol 130:1833-1842",
        "doi": "10.1038/sj.bjp.0703507",
        "prep": "RDL homomer, Drosophila S2 line",
        "value": "E_GABA = -1.4 mV, near the calculated Cl- equilibrium for symmetrical Cl-"
      },
      {
        "cite": "Lee, Su & O'Dowd 2003, J Neurosci 23:4625-4634",
        "prep": "cultured EMBRYONIC Drosophila neurons",
        "value": "x-intercepts -44.5 mV and 0 mV in two internal-Cl conditions, each near the theoretical Cl- equilibrium for that internal"
      },
      {
        "cite": "Rohrbough & Broadie 2002, J Neurophysiol 88:847-860",
        "doi": "10.1152/jn.2002.88.2.847",
        "prep": "LARVAL central neurons",
        "value": "-56 +/- 3 mV in 6 of 9 neurons",
        "note": "full text paywalled (HTTP 403); value from the retrievable quotation and matches the value docs/LIF_DYNAMICS_SPEC.md 3.1 already cites"
      },
      {
        "cite": "Su & O'Dowd 2003, J Neurosci 23:9246-9253",
        "prep": "ADULT Kenyon cells in situ",
        "value": "-37 +/- 3 mV against a theoretical -45 mV for their internal"
      },
      {
        "cite": "Wilson & Laurent 2005, J Neurosci 25:9069-9079",
        "prep": "ADULT antennal lobe, in vivo whole cell",
        "internal": "140 K-aspartate, 10 HEPES, 1 KCl, 4 MgATP, 0.5 Na3GTP, 1 EGTA; external 103 mM NaCl (Nernst E_Cl for that internal is roughly -120 mV)",
        "value": "GABA pulse from threshold (-39 +/- 1 mV) hyperpolarised local-neuron somata to -56 +/- 2 mV",
        "why_it_matters": "the operative endpoint of GABAergic hyperpolarisation in an intact adult central neuron is near -56 mV even under a pipette that should have imposed -120 mV"
      },
      {
        "cite": "Gouwens & Wilson 2009, J Neurosci 29:6239-6249",
        "pmc": "PMC2709801",
        "prep": "ADULT antennal lobe PNs",
        "value": "\"Lowering [Cl-]e did not significantly change the resting membrane potential, so we conclude that there is little chloride current flowing at rest in PNs\"; true resting potential -55 to -60 mV with ORN input, about -65 mV without",
        "why_it_matters": "pipette-independent: little Cl- current at rest implies E_Cl ~ V_rest"
      },
      {
        "cite": "Schellinger et al. 2021/2022, bioRxiv 10.1101/2021.07.16.452737; published as Chloride oscillation in pacemaker neurons regulates circadian rhythms through a chloride-sensing WNK kinase signalling cascade, PMID 35303418",
        "prep": "ADULT sLNv pacemaker neurons, ClopHensor",
        "value": "intracellular Cl- rises and falls across the day, Ncc69-dependently",
        "why_it_matters": "E_Cl in an adult Drosophila neuron is a function of time of day"
      },
      {
        "cite": "Chloride-dependent mechanisms of multimodal sensory discrimination and nociceptive sensitization in Drosophila, eLife 2022, elifesciences.org/articles/76863",
        "value": "kcc down- and ncc69 up-regulated in class III neurons, suggesting relatively high intracellular Cl-",
        "why_it_matters": "E_Cl is also a function of cell type"
      }
    ],
    "glucl": "No separate GluCl reversal potential is reported, and none could be: a Cl--selective channel reverses at E_Cl. Cully et al. 1996 J Biol Chem 271:20187-20191 (PMID 8702744) and Kane et al. 2000 PNAS 97:13949-13954 (doi 10.1073/pnas.240464697) establish GluCl-alpha as a glutamate-gated chloride channel; Liu & Wilson 2013 PNAS 110:10294-10299 shows glutamate is inhibitory in the adult olfactory system. GluCl-alpha supplies NO independent support for -70 mV. Correction of record: the project docs do not cite -70 mV for GluCl-alpha; LIF_DYNAMICS_SPEC 6.3 cites Liu & Wilson only for \"glutamate is inhibitory via a chloride conductance\", and 3.1 already labels -70 mV an engineering assumption.",
    "structural_consequence": "This engine V_rest = -52 mV (Shiu et al. 2024) is ABOVE every measured adult Drosophila resting potential, and the v3 rule g_unit_inh = 1/(V_rest - E_inh) diverges as E_inh approaches V_rest and is undefined for E_inh >= -52 mV. The literature-supported range therefore sits where the declared calibration is most extreme (1/8 at -60 mV, 1/4 at -56 mV vs 1/18 at -70 mV). Declared in advance as a confound, not discovered afterwards."
  },
